# Frontend environment. Copy to `.env.local` (dev) or `.env.production` (the
# single-VPS deploy — see ../.env.production.example and ../nginx/).
#
# Base URL of the FastAPI backend. Three modes:
#
#   1. "same-origin" — the Phase 6 production deployment: Nginx proxies /api
#      on the SAME origin as the page (see ../nginx/balkan-fleet.conf.example).
#      lib/api.ts treats this literally: every call resolves as a plain
#      relative fetch, no host/port guessing at all. Use this in production.
#
#   2. A *loopback* value like the dev default below means "follow the host
#      this page was served from": lib/api.ts swaps in window.location.hostname
#      whenever the page is opened from a LAN address. That is what lets one
#      running server answer localhost and http://<lan-ip>:3000 at the same
#      time (the desktop launcher's LAN mode), so you do NOT need to edit this
#      file (or rebuild) to run on the local network — see README "Run it".
#
#   3. A genuinely remote host (e.g. https://balkan-fleet-api.up.railway.app)
#      is always used exactly as written — the old split-host deployment.
#      lib/api.ts also keeps the Bearer-token fallback alive only for this case.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8001
